<title>VENEZUELA: UK insurance company buys Venezuela's Royal Caribe.</title>
<headline>UK insurance company buys Venezuela's Royal Caribe.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British insurance company Royal International Insurance Holding Ltd acquired a 40 percent stake in Venezuelan Royal Caribe Insurance for 2.4 billion bolivars ($5 million), national State Deposits Guarantee Fund Fogade said on Friday.</p>
<p>Local legal representative Guillermo de la Rosa said Royal International would invest an undisclosed amount in the company which it hoped would become the market leader over the next ten years.</p>
<p>Royal International already counts on a 20 percent share of Royal Caribe, bought in the 1970s.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
